      "writtenOn": "2023-02-22T01:13:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "2K. It looks like `ts_read` always strips the trailing `\\n` from trunks read. If this gets set to 2048 and we generate that much output, the `\\n` doesn\u0027t fit in the buffer and we end up trimming a byte of the response and hit errors.",
      "parentUuid": "846aa993_4668fee5",
      "range": {
